Every clinician should consider a testing-benefit before an opioid-initiation and should consider a testing-risk before an opioid-initiation.
If a patient receives an opioid-therapy during a year then every clinician should consider a testing-benefit during the year and should consider a testing-risk during the year.
A toxicology-testing can assess a prescribed-opioid and can assess a prescribed-controlled-substance and can assess a nonprescribed-controlled-substance and can assess a nonprescribed-opioid and can assess an illicit-opioid and can assess a benzodiazepine.
